meta {
  name: 01 Normal Orientation (pid1)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/chat
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cookie: copilot_session={{copilot_session}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "Give me a quick orientation on this patient: active problems, current meds, and allergies.",
    "patient_id": "98c4b82b-b07e-11f1-8334-022958ad0af8"
  }
}

docs {
  Auth: requires the copilot_session environment variable to be set to a real,
  still-valid session cookie -- see bruno/README.md. Without it this 401s with
  {"detail": "Not logged in..."} regardless of the scenario below.

  pid1 = Alice Testpatient, a normal chart: type 2 diabetes, hypertension,
  Metformin, Lisinopril, an uncoded (narrative-only) Penicillin allergy --
  and a known duplicate record (pid6).

  Look for in the response:
  - Real grounded facts: diabetes, hypertension, metformin, lisinopril,
    penicillin all appear (all real chart data, not fabricated).
  - A duplicate-record warning naming the other matching patient_id.
  - verification_passed: true, flagged_claims: [] (nothing had to be
    stripped -- everything the model said was actually grounded).
}
